From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Karlman <jonas@kwiboo.se>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:07:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3588: Use SCMI GPU clock as the GPU
 core clock

CLK_GPU is the main clock of the RK3588 GPU. Its usual source is one of
gpll, cpll, aupll, npll or spll through an integer divider, and with the
PLL rates set at boot (1188, 1500, 786.432, 850 and 702 MHz) most OPPs
in the GPU table cannot be reached. The rates on an Orange Pi 5 (devfreq
cur_freq under load; 400 MHz from the clock tree) were:

  OPP (MHz)    300  400  500  600  700  800    900  1000
  CLK_GPU      300  396  500  594  594  786.4  850   850

so the 900 and 1000 MHz OPPs ran at 850 MHz with the 1 GHz voltage, and
800 MHz came from the audio PLL.

For higher rates the GPU can also be fed by its PVTPLL. The logic to
switch between a normal PLL and the PVTPLL is in the TF-A firmware and
is exposed to Linux as SCMI_CLK_GPU: TF-A uses GPLL for 200 MHz and the
PVTPLL for every rate from 300 MHz to 1 GHz, which are exactly the
rates of the OPP table.

Use SCMI_CLK_GPU as the GPU core clock, and keep the CRU gate CLK_GPU as
the "bus" clock, as on RK356x.

The PVTPLL and its registers in the GPU GRF are in the GPU power domain,
so the GPU must not be powered down or up while it runs from the
PVTPLL. Add a 200 MHz OPP marked opp-suspend to the RK3588 and RK3588J
GPU tables, at the voltage of their 300 MHz OPP. devfreq then moves the
GPU to the GPLL path before each runtime suspend, and back to the PVTPLL
after resume.

Before this change the GPU clock rate was max 850 MHz:

  [terrain] <default>: FPS: 139 FrameTime: 7.231 ms

After this change the GPU can use the 1 GHz rate with the PVTPLL:

  [terrain] <default>: FPS: 152 FrameTime: 6.579 ms

Signed-off-by: Jonas Karlman <jonas@kwiboo.se>
Link: https://github.com/armbian/linux-rockchip/pull/380
[Ported from the RFC to v7.3 (rk3588-base.dtsi, rk3588-opp.dtsi); also
 add the 200 MHz suspend OPP to rk3588j.dtsi; describe the measured
 CRU rates and the power domain constraint]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi | 10 +++++-----
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-opp.dtsi  |  5 +++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588j.dtsi     |  5 +++++
 3 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
index bdc5cc03a..e61cc868a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
@@ -450,11 +450,11 @@ gpu: gpu@fb000000 {
 		compatible = "rockchip,rk3588-mali", "arm,mali-valhall-csf";
 		reg = <0x0 0xfb000000 0x0 0x200000>;
 		#cooling-cells = <2>;
-		assigned-clocks = <&scmi_clk SCMI_CLK_GPU>;
-		assigned-clock-rates = <200000000>;
-		clocks = <&cru CLK_GPU>, <&cru CLK_GPU_COREGROUP>,
-			 <&cru CLK_GPU_STACKS>;
-		clock-names = "core", "coregroup", "stacks";
+		assigned-clocks = <&cru CLK_GPU>, <&scmi_clk SCMI_CLK_GPU>;
+		assigned-clock-rates = <198000000>, <200000000>;
+		clocks = <&scmi_clk SCMI_CLK_GPU>, <&cru CLK_GPU_COREGROUP>,
+			 <&cru CLK_GPU_STACKS>, <&cru CLK_GPU>;
+		clock-names = "core", "coregroup", "stacks", "bus";
 		dynamic-power-coefficient = <2982>;
 		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 92 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
 			     <GIC_SPI 93 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-opp.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-opp.dtsi
index 59ecaef51..af706f010 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-opp.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-opp.dtsi
@@ -118,6 +118,11 @@ opp-2400000000 {
 	gpu_opp_table: opp-table-gpu {
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
+		opp-200000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <200000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <675000 675000 850000>;
+			opp-suspend;
+		};
 		opp-300000000 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <300000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <675000 675000 850000>;
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588j.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588j.dtsi
index e1e0e3fc0..1ca74d4fb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588j.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588j.dtsi
@@ -69,6 +69,11 @@ opp-1608000000 {
 	gpu_opp_table: opp-table-gpu {
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
+		opp-200000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <200000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <750000 750000 850000>;
+			opp-suspend;
+		};
 		opp-300000000 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <300000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <750000 750000 850000>;
